          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On November 24, 1980, at approximately 10:20 PM, a motorist observed a white-light point in the clear sky for one second. It moved from west to east along a straight trajectory, at an angle between 30° and 60° above the horizon. It disappeared instantly. No unusual noises were heard during the observation. No further information was gathered on this phenomenon, for which we have limited data.",
